# Local Pi runtime state
.atl/

# Secrets — DB credentials, WordPress salts, Cloudflare tunnel token.
# wp-config.php is GENERATED by reset-rebuild.sh and embeds random salts.
.env
wp-config.php

# Build artifact: rebuilt by ./build-zip.sh from webp-studio/.
webp-studio.zip

# Staging database analysis environment.
#
# analysis/ holds the compose file and the query helpers, which are safe to keep.
# analysis/.env holds the STAGING DATABASE PASSWORD and must never be committed.
analysis/.env

# Scratch files from earlier debugging sessions (unreferenced by any config).
temp_method.php
temp_stats.php
large.png
test.jpg
test.png
valid.png
docker-compose.yml.backup

# Browser-automation artifacts from the Playwright MCP session.
.playwright-mcp/

# Seed images.
#
# The image binaries are ignored; seed.sh and README.md stay tracked because they are the
# regeneration path. The fixtures themselves weigh ~17 MB and would dominate the history
# for no benefit: they are development fixtures, not plugin assets or release artifacts.
#
# The dev environment still depends on them at runtime (reset-rebuild.sh destroys the
# WordPress volume and re-imports them, so a fresh clone boots with a real media
# library). Regenerate them after cloning with:
#
#     seed-images/seed.sh --download
#
# The download uses fixed Lorem Picsum IDs, so the result is byte-for-byte reproducible.
# See seed-images/README.md.
seed-images/**/*.jpg
seed-images/**/*.jpeg
seed-images/**/*.png
seed-images/**/*.gif
seed-images/**/*.webp
seed-images/**/*.avif

# Third-party security scanner, cloned locally from https://github.com/duriantaco/skylos.
#
# It was briefly tracked as a gitlink (mode 160000) with no .gitmodules, which pointed at
# a commit that only existed inside the nested clone. Nothing in this repository invokes
# it — no script, no CI job, no doc — so it is a developer tool, not a dependency of the
# plugin. A submodule would wrongly claim this project depends on it, so it stays local.
# Re-clone into this path if you need to re-run the audit: git clone <url> skylos
/skylos/

# PyPA's official pip bootstrap, vendored for a one-off audit run. No file in this
# repository references it, and it embeds a base85 copy of all of pip (2.2 MB).
get-pip.py

# odd/ holds AI-orchestration task-tracking documents (feature objectives, checklists,
# commit receipts). They are process artifacts, not part of the plugin or its build.
odd/